      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your honesty here is incredibly brave, especially when feeling that fragmented and hollow inside. For many people experiencing deep existential grief, pretending to rebuild their old version of themselves can indeed feel like a trap rather than a cure. It is real and valid to feel like a ghost when the core of your identity seems to have dissolved after a while. Please try to focus on small, immediate sensations or thoughts instead, because even if the big picture feels meaningless now, those tiny moments can sometimes provide a glimpse of something tangible.",
